# App (`apps/app`)

Docs: `doc/features/ui-system.md`, `doc/features/authentication.md`.

## Layout

```text
src/app/                 # App Router pages / layouts
src/features/<feature>/  # schemas, store, hooks
src/components/          # UI composition
src/lib/                 # api clients, auth helpers, store
```

## Conventions

- Prefer feature folders under `src/features/` for domain state and schemas.
- Use `@saas-boilerplate/ui` / shared Tailwind patterns; don’t invent a parallel design system.
- Talk to the API via existing clients (axios / feature hooks); don’t bypass auth cookies casually.
- Never hardcode credentials, demo passwords, or secrets in client components (they ship to the browser).
- Admin UI must not imply stronger auth than the API enforces; treat client gates as UX only.
- Match existing Redux / store patterns in `src/features` and `src/lib/store.ts`.

## Tests

- Component/unit tests with Vitest where the codebase already tests similar UI.
